WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.733 --> 00:00:08.033
- This way.
- Clemont, wait up!

2
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.100
Come on, stragglers. Move.

3
00:00:10.166 --> 00:00:14.166
- I've never seen Clemont run this quickly.
- Slow it down a little.

4
00:00:14.233 --> 00:00:15.600
Pika!

5
00:00:16.366 --> 00:00:18.100
There. That's it, all right.

6
00:00:18.166 --> 00:00:21.933
There's no doubt. The Gadget Festival is just up ahead.

7
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.333
It's the largest exhibition of mechanical devices

8
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.433
in the entire Kalos region.

9
00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:29.900
All this running for that?

10
00:00:29.966 --> 00:00:33.733
- It's that great?
- Calling it great would be an insult.

11
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.366
All of the most brilliant and talented inventors from Kalos

12
00:00:37.433 --> 00:00:40.500
will compete by showing all their mechanical wares.

13
00:00:40.566 --> 00:00:41.966
- Wow!
- Pika!

14
00:00:42.033 --> 00:00:45.500
- And that's more than great?
- Well, you just wait and see.

15
00:00:45.566 --> 00:00:48.633
- What are you waiting for?
- Sounds like a lot of fun.

16
00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:49.566
Pika, Pika.

17
00:00:51.633 --> 00:00:53.300
This is it.

18
00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.400
Wow, it's huge.

19
00:00:59.366 --> 00:01:02.400
So, this is what they call the Gadget Festival.

20
00:01:02.466 --> 00:01:04.866
- Awesome.
- Dedenne.

21
00:01:04.933 --> 00:01:09.866
That's right. The best and brightest, all gathered in one magnificent setting.

22
00:01:09.933 --> 00:01:12.033
Unbelievable.

23
00:01:13.766 --> 00:01:18.866
Even the word "gadget" is inspiring. A triumph of human intelligence and skill.

24
00:01:18.933 --> 00:01:22.733
The gears of my curiosity are turning like there's no tomorrow,

25
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:24.866
and they're not about to stop.

26
00:01:29.933 --> 00:01:33.233
♪ I stand tall 'Cause I know I'm a winner ♪

27
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.166
♪ Knock me down I'll just get up again ♪

28
00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:41.066
♪ You've met your match Yeah, I'm no beginner ♪

29
00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:43.733
♪ Pokémon, Pokémon ♪

30
00:01:44.333 --> 00:01:45.466
♪ Gotta catch 'em all ♪

31
00:01:45.533 --> 00:01:48.633
♪ I stand tall 'Cause I know I'm a winner ♪

32
00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:51.866
♪ Pokémon, Pokémon ♪

33
00:01:51.933 --> 00:01:53.600
♪ Gotta catch 'em all ♪

34
00:02:12.733 --> 00:02:14.933
Right. Just do it like that.

35
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.933
Yippee! This is so cool.

36
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:25.266
- Huh? What's that?
- You're looking at the welcome gadget.

37
00:02:25.333 --> 00:02:29.266
It will help to explain exactly what a gadget is about with ease.

38
00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:34.000
- Looks complicated.
- So, how does this thing even work?

39
00:02:34.066 --> 00:02:34.933
Pika, Pika.

40
00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:38.200
We simply place a ball in here, and...

41
00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:08.633
- It's still going.
- Wow, gadgets are so amazing.

42
00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:09.900
Pika, Pika!

43
00:03:09.966 --> 00:03:12.200
Can't wait to see what happens next.

44
00:03:28.166 --> 00:03:33.066
Genius. It's an automatic berry-opener. Inspiration plus.

45
00:03:33.133 --> 00:03:35.533
Seems like a waste of time.

46
00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:36.566
Why build that?

47
00:03:38.966 --> 00:03:41.166
Isn't doing this a whole lot easier?

48
00:03:42.566 --> 00:03:46.800
Nonsense. You don't get it. Gadgets have a sense of playfulness.

49
00:03:46.866 --> 00:03:49.966
Playfulness creates a variety of inventions,

50
00:03:50.033 --> 00:03:52.166
which leads to new technologies.

51
00:03:52.233 --> 00:03:56.866
The lives of convenience we live are built upon this foundation of gadgets.

52
00:03:56.966 --> 00:04:01.500
The name of the game is fun. Otherwise, you'll never be able to appreciate

53
00:04:01.566 --> 00:04:05.500
- all this wonderful place has to offer.
- So, this is about fun.

54
00:04:05.566 --> 00:04:06.766
Whee.

55
00:04:06.833 --> 00:04:08.300
That makes sense to me.

56
00:04:08.366 --> 00:04:09.466
Pikachu.

57
00:04:09.533 --> 00:04:12.500
Fun, fun, fun. Here we come.

58
00:04:17.266 --> 00:04:21.066
There. I've just completed my Poké Ball Stealer Mark One.

59
00:04:21.533 --> 00:04:24.766
So, now everyone's Poké Balls will be our Poké Balls.

60
00:04:24.833 --> 00:04:28.166
Right. All that remains is a teensy bit of a fine-tune.

61
00:04:28.233 --> 00:04:33.133
- So, this is your gadget room?
- It certainly is. Something wrong?

62
00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:36.933
Isn't a gadget what people use to keep track of money?

63
00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.533
You know what I mean. A household gadget.

64
00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:41.633
No, that's a budget, brainiac.

65
00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:44.566
- There's a difference?
- Like night and day.

66
00:04:44.633 --> 00:04:45.866
Oh.

67
00:04:45.933 --> 00:04:50.366
Let's go to the gadget rooms and discover what the others came up with.

68
00:04:50.433 --> 00:04:53.366
- Check the competition.
- Right behind you.

69
00:04:53.433 --> 00:04:57.366
Please. Gadget, budget. Who cares?

70
00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:03.366
Sit in one of these chairs and it will take you up.

71
00:05:03.433 --> 00:05:04.466
Yay!

72
00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:07.200
Now, you be careful.

73
00:05:07.933 --> 00:05:08.900
I will.

74
00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:12.033
I think we should go, too. Huh?

75
00:05:13.366 --> 00:05:14.900
Chespin! Chespin!

76
00:05:14.966 --> 00:05:16.966
Chespin wants to ride up with us.

77
00:05:17.033 --> 00:05:20.200
I'll bet Pancham would, too. This'll be fun.

78
00:05:21.633 --> 00:05:22.766
- Che?
- Pancham.

79
00:05:30.066 --> 00:05:33.466
- Twerps and Pikachu.
- I think we can catch Pikachu

80
00:05:33.533 --> 00:05:36.300
before we use the Poké Ball Stealer Mark One.

81
00:05:36.366 --> 00:05:37.200
Hear, hear.

82
00:05:37.266 --> 00:05:40.466
The gadget rooms should provide ample opportunities.

83
00:05:40.533 --> 00:05:43.200
- They don't want to waste money.
- Wrong word.

84
00:05:45.266 --> 00:05:47.700
- Huh? Must be locked.
- Give it a push.

85
00:05:49.066 --> 00:05:50.166
It's stuck.

86
00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:53.833
I know. Pull it to the side.

87
00:05:54.933 --> 00:05:55.833
You're right.

88
00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:59.066
That's the way with gimmicks. I love them.

89
00:05:59.966 --> 00:06:01.700
Man, a wall.

90
00:06:01.766 --> 00:06:04.600
So it seems. Let's just see.

91
00:06:08.366 --> 00:06:10.200
It was really a hidden door.

92
00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:13.566
Hey. Pikachu and the others are gone.

93
00:06:15.666 --> 00:06:16.766
Pikachu?

94
00:06:18.066 --> 00:06:21.300
We've gotten separated, so, let's meet up later.

95
00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:24.400
- That okay, buddy?
- Pikachu!

96
00:06:24.466 --> 00:06:25.633
You be good.

97
00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:27.933
Now let's go this way.

98
00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:31.133
So, it looks like we gotta get over those next, huh?

99
00:06:37.733 --> 00:06:40.166
- Dedenne.
- Here I come.

100
00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:42.800
Dedenne!

101
00:06:43.966 --> 00:06:44.800
Now.

102
00:06:45.833 --> 00:06:47.800
That's the way to do it, Bonnie.

103
00:06:48.433 --> 00:06:49.333
This is fun.

104
00:06:50.900 --> 00:06:51.900
Whoa.

105
00:06:51.966 --> 00:06:53.666
Way to go, Clemont.

106
00:06:53.733 --> 00:06:55.800
You're like a totally different person today.

107
00:06:55.866 --> 00:06:57.533
Ta-da!

108
00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.366
Okay, let's keep it up.

109
00:07:20.833 --> 00:07:22.400
- Pika!
- Pin!

110
00:07:35.266 --> 00:07:37.500
Must be a trick to this door, too.

111
00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:42.466
It feels like it's been glued shut.

112
00:07:42.533 --> 00:07:45.433
Let me try it now.

113
00:07:47.166 --> 00:07:48.266
Huh?

114
00:07:48.333 --> 00:07:50.800
So, that's the way the door works.

115
00:07:51.966 --> 00:07:53.100
Whoa!

116
00:07:57.666 --> 00:08:00.966
- This thing's broke.
- If it doesn't pull, try pushing.

117
00:08:02.366 --> 00:08:04.100
That doesn't work, either.

118
00:08:04.566 --> 00:08:06.633
Now watch the master at work.

119
00:08:07.433 --> 00:08:08.666
Voilà.

120
00:08:09.266 --> 00:08:10.833
The annoying master.

121
00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:14.900
- What is this stupid contraption?
- That's a wall.

122
00:08:16.333 --> 00:08:17.633
It's elementary.

123
00:08:19.533 --> 00:08:22.666
- Open sesame.
- You're still annoying.

124
00:08:50.366 --> 00:08:51.533
Pika, Pika.

125
00:08:52.766 --> 00:08:54.600
I heard Pikachu down below.

126
00:08:58.533 --> 00:08:59.466
My bad.

127
00:09:04.066 --> 00:09:06.000
-Ah.

128
00:09:07.166 --> 00:09:08.900
Balancing a household budget

129
00:09:08.966 --> 00:09:12.100
- makes me glad I don't have a house.
- It's a gadget.

130
00:09:12.766 --> 00:09:15.166
Sliding down was the right thing to do.

131
00:09:17.266 --> 00:09:19.933
I think you're supposed to sit on this thing.

132
00:09:24.133 --> 00:09:27.033
Whoa! Yeah!

133
00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.733
- It stopped.
- Now, that's a great gadget.

134
00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:34.000
- Like an amusement park.
- Dedenne.

135
00:09:34.066 --> 00:09:35.033
Huh?

136
00:09:36.666 --> 00:09:37.533
Now what?

137
00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:41.033
- Clemont?
- Maybe another arm appears.

138
00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:42.633
Well, I can't wait.

139
00:09:43.933 --> 00:09:45.033
Whoa!

140
00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:48.066
Good thing you didn't wait.

141
00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:55.800
- Bonnie. Hurry. Hurry.
- Don't worry. I know.

142
00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:58.033
Whoa. That thing doesn't waste time.

143
00:09:58.566 --> 00:10:01.066
This will be like a walk in the park.

144
00:10:03.566 --> 00:10:05.600
We've got to catch up to Pikachu.

145
00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:13.100
This is getting so old.

146
00:10:13.166 --> 00:10:16.700
- Stop! No more! My back!
- Oy vey, Jess.

147
00:10:18.233 --> 00:10:19.200
Huh?

148
00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:21.233
What's that?

149
00:10:26.766 --> 00:10:30.000
Wow. That's the cutest little wind-up doll I've ever seen.

150
00:10:30.066 --> 00:10:32.600
- Yeah, it's so well made.
- Adorable.

151
00:10:32.666 --> 00:10:34.166
It's built really well.

152
00:10:36.366 --> 00:10:38.700
Want me to have a cup of tea?

153
00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:41.200
That's hot. What was that for?

154
00:10:41.733 --> 00:10:44.366
I'm guessing that was a little bit of humor.

155
00:10:44.766 --> 00:10:47.033
-That's part of the playfulness.

156
00:10:49.733 --> 00:10:50.766
Huh?

157
00:10:54.666 --> 00:10:57.233
It's obvious from the lovely way she bowed

158
00:10:57.300 --> 00:11:00.266
- her manners are second to none.
- If you say so.

159
00:11:26.033 --> 00:11:27.300
Pika.

160
00:11:33.866 --> 00:11:37.466
- Where did Pikachu get to now?
- Further ahead, I'd say.

161
00:11:37.533 --> 00:11:40.466
Ah. Perfect. I needed a rest.

162
00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:45.400
This feels pretty good.

163
00:11:46.733 --> 00:11:48.000
Huh?

164
00:11:48.066 --> 00:11:51.266
- What's going on?
- Perhaps another arm will manifest.

165
00:11:51.333 --> 00:11:52.966
Oh, yeah? From where, then?

166
00:11:56.366 --> 00:11:57.200
Man.

167
00:11:58.133 --> 00:12:02.800
- That little doll's a little doll.
- And it's well-known all over the region.

168
00:12:02.866 --> 00:12:07.033
- How nice. You brought us tea, didn't you?
- Thanks for the refreshments.

169
00:12:09.233 --> 00:12:11.366
My tongue turned into burnt toast.

170
00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:15.900
We'll never catch Pikachu trapped inside this loony bin.

171
00:12:15.966 --> 00:12:18.900
Why don't we chill out and get my tongue some ice?

172
00:12:18.966 --> 00:12:22.866
So, it's time we employ our Poké Ball Stealer Mark One.

173
00:12:22.933 --> 00:12:24.033
For fun.

174
00:12:27.233 --> 00:12:29.166
Who's that Pokémon?

175
00:12:33.933 --> 00:12:35.800
It's Pinsir.

176
00:12:44.966 --> 00:12:46.666
Welcome, child.

177
00:12:46.733 --> 00:12:48.566
What's up with this room?

178
00:12:48.633 --> 00:12:51.600
You've wandered into the Poké Ball Budget Room.

179
00:12:51.666 --> 00:12:53.366
She means Gadget Room.

180
00:12:53.433 --> 00:12:55.266
What's it got to do with Poké Balls?

181
00:12:55.333 --> 00:12:58.166
You place your Poké Ball right in there.

182
00:12:58.533 --> 00:12:59.366
Like this?

183
00:13:01.866 --> 00:13:04.933
I'm afraid that's not quite enough weight just yet.

184
00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:08.800
Third ball's the charm.

185
00:13:11.266 --> 00:13:12.800
- It's moving.
- Awesome.

186
00:13:19.366 --> 00:13:21.633
Now watch as they separate into three directions.

187
00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:22.533
Whoa!

188
00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:34.366
And finally they've reunited.

189
00:13:34.433 --> 00:13:35.366
Oh, wow!

190
00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:41.433
Um... uh...

191
00:13:42.133 --> 00:13:43.700
Where are my Poké Balls?

192
00:13:44.666 --> 00:13:46.466
Not your concern. Bye-bye.

193
00:13:54.966 --> 00:13:57.766
- All right!
- Poké Ball Stealer Mark One rules.

194
00:13:57.833 --> 00:14:00.466
- And everyone else drools.
- Those fools.

195
00:14:02.833 --> 00:14:04.200
Welcome, child.

196
00:14:04.666 --> 00:14:05.800
Wow. What room is this?

197
00:14:05.866 --> 00:14:07.966
You wandered into the right place.

198
00:14:08.033 --> 00:14:09.900
The Poké Ball Gadget Room.

199
00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:15.933
- But wait. Nothing happened.
- Third ball's the charm.

200
00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:16.900
One more?

201
00:14:17.300 --> 00:14:18.400
- Success.
- Yay!

202
00:14:21.166 --> 00:14:23.333
Watch as they separate into three directions.

203
00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:24.233
Wow!

204
00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:29.133
And finally they've reunited.

205
00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:34.600
Hey, where are my Poké Balls? They're gone.

206
00:14:35.166 --> 00:14:37.166
Not your concern. Bye-bye.

207
00:14:44.100 --> 00:14:46.300
- Pika, Pi!
- Huh? Pikachu!

208
00:14:46.366 --> 00:14:48.000
- Pika, Pika!
- Pancham!

209
00:14:48.066 --> 00:14:50.200
- Cham, Cham!
- Did everybody have fun?

210
00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:55.700
8

211
00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:57.200
Pika!

212
00:14:57.266 --> 00:14:59.133
Hey, guys. Cut it out.

213
00:15:00.766 --> 00:15:03.966
- Huh? No, not in this room.
- Is something the matter?

214
00:15:04.033 --> 00:15:07.766
We had several reports of Poké Balls being stolen in the area.

215
00:15:08.233 --> 00:15:09.733
Poké Balls being stolen?

216
00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:12.800
- That's just awful.
- Let's have a look around.

217
00:15:15.033 --> 00:15:16.000
My Poké Balls!

218
00:15:16.466 --> 00:15:18.633
- What are you doing?
- What's going on here?

219
00:15:19.866 --> 00:15:23.033
My Poké Balls just went down that thing.

220
00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:24.100
Hold on.

221
00:15:28.966 --> 00:15:30.200
Down that pipe?

222
00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:33.566
Yeah, that's it.

223
00:15:36.866 --> 00:15:39.800
What are you doing in this Gadget Room anyway?

224
00:15:39.866 --> 00:15:43.966
All the world is a stage. Budgets are an actor's tools of the trade.

225
00:15:44.033 --> 00:15:46.800
- Whatever.
- Allow us to reveal our charade.

226
00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:53.600
- To protect the world from devastation.
- To unite all people within our nation.

227
00:15:53.666 --> 00:15:56.433
To ease on down the Poké Ball stealing road.

228
00:15:56.500 --> 00:15:59.766
To extend our reach till we've grabbed the last load.

229
00:16:00.266 --> 00:16:01.933
- Jessie.
- And James.

230
00:16:02.566 --> 00:16:05.500
Team Rocket blasts off at the speed of light.

231
00:16:05.566 --> 00:16:08.600
Surrender now or prepare for a gadget-laden fight.

232
00:16:08.666 --> 00:16:10.066
Meowth, that's right.

233
00:16:12.100 --> 00:16:15.066
- Team Rocket!
- Give the Poké Balls back.

234
00:16:15.133 --> 00:16:17.133
- Not today.
- And away.

235
00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:19.633
Come back.

236
00:16:23.366 --> 00:16:25.233
- This is fun.
- Dedenne!

237
00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:27.766
Bonnie, be careful.

238
00:16:29.433 --> 00:16:30.400
Stop!

239
00:16:31.333 --> 00:16:32.300
Whoo.

240
00:16:32.366 --> 00:16:35.900
You're not hoofing it now like you have two left feet.

241
00:16:35.966 --> 00:16:40.433
Thank you. My true brilliance doesn't come out until I'm under pressure.

242
00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:42.000
That's how genius works.

243
00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:48.033
- I told her not to scoff at gadgets.
- Come back.

244
00:16:49.833 --> 00:16:51.000
Pika!

245
00:16:51.066 --> 00:16:51.900
Yes!

246
00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:54.733
Stop!

247
00:16:56.033 --> 00:16:57.866
Those Poké Balls aren't yours.

248
00:16:58.333 --> 00:17:02.500
- We've been hustling with budgets.
- It's gadgets, genius.

249
00:17:02.566 --> 00:17:04.466
Now go for it, Meowth.

250
00:17:05.233 --> 00:17:06.066
Roger.

251
00:17:08.133 --> 00:17:09.933
- What's going on?
- Pika?

252
00:17:11.599 --> 00:17:12.933
Feast your eyes.

253
00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:16.066
We worked on this for three days and three nights,

254
00:17:16.133 --> 00:17:18.466
without sleeping. Our greatest work.

255
00:17:18.533 --> 00:17:22.733
Our monstrous, megalomaniacal, super-attacking, gilded Meowth gadget.

256
00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:26.333
Excellent. That's a really impressive piece of work.

257
00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:30.766
Show them what it can do. Stop, drop and roll.

258
00:18:03.733 --> 00:18:08.133
- This is a budget that walks the walk.
- It's "gadget." Learn how to talk.

259
00:18:16.733 --> 00:18:17.566
Ah!

260
00:18:18.433 --> 00:18:19.666
Now for fury swipes.

261
00:18:20.433 --> 00:18:21.433
Pi!

262
00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:23.766
-Pi?

263
00:18:26.433 --> 00:18:27.933
Pika, Pikachu.

264
00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:38.233
It would have been simpler for Meowth to just use fury swipes.

265
00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:39.966
That silly thing didn't even reach.

266
00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:42.933
Nonsense! Stop it!

267
00:18:43.000 --> 00:18:45.566
Gadgets should have a sense of playfulness.

268
00:18:45.633 --> 00:18:48.933
It's vital to the very reason for this machine's brilliance.

269
00:18:49.000 --> 00:18:50.166
Mm-hm.

270
00:18:50.233 --> 00:18:53.666
This is the first time I've agreed with Team Rocket, wow.

271
00:18:53.733 --> 00:18:56.166
Hey, those are the bad guys.

272
00:18:56.633 --> 00:18:59.000
Give the Poké Balls back or you'll be sorry.

273
00:18:59.066 --> 00:19:00.066
Boohoo.

274
00:19:00.133 --> 00:19:02.633
- Get them, Gourgeist.
- Okay, Inkay.

275
00:19:05.033 --> 00:19:06.733
- Gourgeist.
- Inkay, Ink.

276
00:19:07.233 --> 00:19:08.833
Now. Seed bomb. Go.

277
00:19:11.933 --> 00:19:13.100
Use psybeam.

278
00:19:13.166 --> 00:19:14.733
Inkay!

279
00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:18.600
Pancham, dark pulse.

280
00:19:18.666 --> 00:19:20.933
Pancham!

281
00:19:21.400 --> 00:19:22.466
Dodge it, quick.

282
00:19:25.033 --> 00:19:26.166
Our gadget!

283
00:19:26.233 --> 00:19:28.500
Now, Chespin. Pin missile.

284
00:19:29.033 --> 00:19:31.800
Chespin!

285
00:19:33.033 --> 00:19:34.133
Oh, no.

286
00:19:35.733 --> 00:19:39.033
All right, Pikachu. Thunderbolt. Let's move it.

287
00:19:39.100 --> 00:19:43.400
Pikachu!

288
00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:53.733
I guess I'll never understand what you all see in those silly gadgets.

289
00:19:53.800 --> 00:19:57.866
- So juvenile.
- You hear that? She didn't say "budget."

290
00:19:57.933 --> 00:20:02.533
Gadgets are a game for the playful. Though I wish this could be, as well.

291
00:20:02.600 --> 00:20:05.166
We're blasting off again!

292
00:20:06.166 --> 00:20:07.333
Inkay.

293
00:20:11.933 --> 00:20:14.266
Here you go. Your Poké Balls are safe.

294
00:20:14.333 --> 00:20:15.600
That's awesome.

295
00:20:15.666 --> 00:20:17.266
- Thanks.
- You were great.

296
00:20:17.333 --> 00:20:20.766
- Looks like a happy ending.
- Glad that's over with.

297
00:20:20.833 --> 00:20:21.866
Then let's go.

298
00:20:22.333 --> 00:20:25.133
There are still lots of Gadget Exhibition Rooms

299
00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:26.866
to explore and enjoy.

300
00:20:26.933 --> 00:20:28.533
Let's go, buddy.

301
00:20:28.600 --> 00:20:30.166
- Pikachu.
- Yay!

302
00:20:32.766 --> 00:20:35.633
Gadgets. The height of irresistibility.

303
00:20:35.700 --> 00:20:40.366
A triumph of human intelligence and skill. The Gadget Festival will celebrate

304
00:20:40.433 --> 00:20:43.066
the world's hopes and dreams for the future,

305
00:20:43.133 --> 00:20:44.933
as the journey continues.
